Example.Output:
## Plan
1. **State Architecture**: `pokemonSlice` with `initialState: { pokemons: [], status: 'idle', error: null }` where `status` is one of `idle | loading | succeeded | failed`. A single status field rather than a `loading` boolean, because two booleans admit a fourth combination nobody intended: with `loading: false` and `pokemons: []`, the very first render, before `useEffect` has dispatched anything, satisfies the empty-state branch and flashes "No Pokemon found" before the spinner appears. Thunk: `fetchPokemons`. Selectors: `selectPokemons`, `selectStatus`, `selectError`.
2. **API Integration**: Axios GET to `https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon?limit=20`. Map each result to `{ id, name, image }`, parsing the id out of `result.url` (`.../pokemon/25/` -> `25`) rather than from the array index. The index happens to equal the id only at `offset=0`; deriving from the URL is what the API actually guarantees and is what keeps this correct the moment pagination is added.
3. **Component Hierarchy**: `App` (Provider + Layout) -> `PokemonList` (useDispatch + useSelector) -> AntD `List` grid -> `List.Item` -> `Card` with `cover` prop for sprite image. `rowKey` set to `id`.
4. **Data Flow**: `useEffect` dispatches `fetchPokemons` on mount -> thunk -> `extraReducers` (pending sets status `loading`, fulfilled sets status `succeeded` and pokemons, rejected sets status `failed` and error) -> `useSelector` reads state -> `List` renders.
5. **Accessibility**:
   - Keyboard: no custom interactive elements; the retry control is a native AntD `Button`, which renders a real `button` and is reachable and operable without extra wiring. `Card hoverable` is presentational only and is deliberately not made clickable, since a clickable card would need a real button or link inside it rather than a click handler on the div.
   - Focus: on transition from `loading` to `failed`, focus moves to the error region via a ref and an effect, so a keyboard user lands on the failure and its retry button instead of being left on a node that no longer exists.
   - Announcement: the error `Alert` is wrapped in a container with `role="alert"` set explicitly rather than trusted to the library, and the list region carries `aria-busy={status === 'loading'}` plus `aria-live="polite"` so the arrival of results is announced. The live region is rendered in all states, not mounted alongside its content, because a live region inserted at the same moment as its text announces nothing.
   - Names: each sprite `img` gets `alt={name}` (informative, it is the only identification of the row for a screen reader user); the page has exactly one `h1`; the retry button's text is its accessible name.
   - Contrast, computed: page background `#f5f5f5`. Body text `#595959` on `#f5f5f5` = 6.42:1, passes AA for normal text. The heading is left at AntD's near-black default rather than a softer grey, because `#8c8c8c` on this background computes to 3.08:1 and fails. Note explicitly: AntD v5's primary `#1677ff` on white is 4.10:1, which fails AA for normal text, so it is used here only for the button's fill behind white text, never as a text color on a light background.
6. **Versions and Cost**: Targets React 18 (`createRoot`; note StrictMode double-invokes effects in development, which is why the thunk is idempotent and guarded on `status === 'idle'`), Ant Design v5 (`antd/dist/reset.css`; v4's `antd/dist/antd.css` is a different file and mixing the two is a common failure), Redux Toolkit 2.x, Axios 1.x. Confirm the AntD `List` grid prop signature against the v5 release notes if the installed minor differs. Cost note: AntD is heavy for a single list, and the stack specifies it, so it is used as specified; a no-dependency version would be a CSS grid and roughly 200 lines less shipped JavaScript.
7. **Consolidation**: Single index.js, Imports -> Slice -> Store -> PokemonList -> App -> ReactDOM render.
8. **Edge Cases**: `idle` (pre-dispatch) renders the same skeleton as `loading` so no empty state can flash; empty successful response renders AntD `Empty`; network error renders `Alert type="error"` with a retry; sprite images that 404 fall back via `onError` rather than rendering a broken-image icon with useless alt text.

## Solution
```javascript
import React, { useEffect, useRef } from 'react';
import ReactDOM from 'react-dom/client';
import { createSlice, createAsyncThunk, configureStore } from '@reduxjs/toolkit';
import { Provider, useDispatch, useSelector } from 'react-redux';
import { List, Card, Spin, Alert, Layout, Empty, Button } from 'antd';
import axios from 'axios';
import 'antd/dist/reset.css';

// --- Constants ---------------------------------------------
const API_URL = 'https://pokeapi.co/api/v2/pokemon?limit=20';
const SPRITE_BASE = 'https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon';
const PAGE_BG = '#f5f5f5';
const TEXT_COLOR = '#595959'; // 6.42:1 on #f5f5f5, passes WCAG AA normal text

// --- Redux Slice ------------------------------------------
const idFromUrl = (url) => url.split('/').filter(Boolean).pop();

const fetchPokemons = createAsyncThunk('pokemon/fetchAll', async () => {
  const { data } = await axios.get(API_URL);
  return data.results.map((p) => {
    const id = idFromUrl(p.url);
    return { id, name: p.name, image: `${SPRITE_BASE}/${id}.png` };
  });
});

const pokemonSlice = createSlice({
  name: 'pokemon',
  initialState: { pokemons: [], status: 'idle', error: null },
  reducers: {},
  extraReducers: (builder) => {
    builder
      .addCase(fetchPokemons.pending, (state) => { state.status = 'loading'; state.error = null; })
      .addCase(fetchPokemons.fulfilled, (state, action) => { state.status = 'succeeded'; state.pokemons = action.payload; })
      .addCase(fetchPokemons.rejected, (state, action) => { state.status = 'failed'; state.error = action.error.message; });
  },
});

const selectPokemons = (state) => state.pokemon.pokemons;
const selectStatus = (state) => state.pokemon.status;
const selectError = (state) => state.pokemon.error;

// --- Store Configuration ------------------------------------
const store = configureStore({ reducer: { pokemon: pokemonSlice.reducer } });

// --- Components -----------------------------------------------
const PokemonList = () => {
  const dispatch = useDispatch();
  const pokemons = useSelector(selectPokemons);
  const status = useSelector(selectStatus);
  const error = useSelector(selectError);
  const errorRef = useRef(null);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (status === 'idle') dispatch(fetchPokemons());
  }, [status, dispatch]);

  useEffect(() => {
    if (status === 'failed' && errorRef.current) errorRef.current.focus();
  }, [status]);

  const busy = status === 'idle' || status === 'loading';

  return (
    <div aria-live="polite" aria-busy={busy}>
      {status === 'failed' && (
        <div role="alert" ref={errorRef} tabIndex={-1}>
          <Alert
            type="error"
            showIcon
            message="Failed to load Pokemon"
            description={error}
            action={<Button size="small" onClick={() => dispatch(fetchPokemons())}>Retry</Button>}
          />
        </div>
      )}
      {status === 'succeeded' && pokemons.length === 0 && (
        <Empty description="No Pokemon found" />
      )}
      {(busy || (status === 'succeeded' && pokemons.length > 0)) && (
        <Spin spinning={busy} size="large">
          <List
            grid={{ gutter: 16, xs: 1, sm: 2, md: 3, lg: 4 }}
            dataSource={pokemons}
            rowKey={(item) => item.id}
            renderItem={(item) => (
              <List.Item>
                <Card cover={<img alt={item.name} src={item.image} style={{ padding: 8 }} />}>
                  <Card.Meta title={item.name.charAt(0).toUpperCase() + item.name.slice(1)} />
                </Card>
              </List.Item>
            )}
          />
        </Spin>
      )}
    </div>
  );
};

// --- App Root ---------------------------------------------------
const App = () => (
  <Provider store={store}>
    <Layout style={{ padding: 24, minHeight: '100vh', background: PAGE_BG }}>
      <Layout.Content style={{ color: TEXT_COLOR }}>
        <h1 style={{ marginBottom: 24, color: 'rgba(0,0,0,0.88)' }}>Pokemon Explorer</h1>
        <PokemonList />
      </Layout.Content>
    </Layout>
  </Provider>
);

ReactDOM.createRoot(document.getElementById('root')).render(<App />);
```

